{
 "format": 2,
 "id": "converter-draw-share",
 "rev": 1,
 "name": "Converters pay only for their share, and Conversion Loss costs power",
 "description": "Written against upstream 459e423 (TrueGrid 1.3.5). Each TrueGrid machine's input draw is now its share of each output circuit's consumption (consumed x own base production / circuit produced) instead of the whole circuit's consumption, in both the main draw loop and the inductor Smoothing Timer. Conversion Loss now multiplies the draw by (2 - Conversion % Penalty) instead of the penalty itself. Ship together: the conversion fix alone would make parallel setups draw more.",
